# Streaming refactor #11 chunk 7 peak-RSS bench meta
date: 2026-05-18
commit: chunk-7-WIP (atop 95623da3 chunk-6 dispatch)
host: $(hostname)
example_default: jxl-encoder/examples/bench_buffering_rss.rs (default LossyConfig::encode())
example_rate_control: jxl-encoder/examples/bench_buffering_rss_rate_control.rs (VarDctEncoder::encode_with_rate_control_config)
build: cargo build --release -p jxl-encoder [--features rate-control for rate-control bench]
measurement: /usr/bin/time -v "Maximum resident set size (kbytes)"

# Chunk 7 honest-stop summary
# ===========================
#
# CHUNK 7 AS-SPECIFIED IS STRUCTURALLY BLOCKED.
# The chunk-3/4/5/6 helpers do NOT produce a peak-RSS reduction on the
# default path because:
#
#   1. `EncoderPrecomputedGlobal::compute_global_only` ALLOCATES an
#      additional `xyb_pre_gaborish` snapshot ([Vec<f32>; 3]) when
#      gaborish is enabled (precomputed.rs:782). That's ~192 MiB EXTRA
#      at 4K — the cost of letting per-region precompute reads from a
#      stable pre-gaborish source. The default `encode_inner` path does
#      gaborish in-place (no snapshot), so routing through
#      `compute_with_budget_and_buffering` would INCREASE peak RSS, not
#      decrease it. The rate-control 4K measurement confirms:
#        FullBuffered:   4441 MiB
#        BufferedOutput: 4759 MiB (+7%)
#      The +7% gap reproduces what chunk-6's 3K bench showed (+12%).
#
#   2. The chunk-4 `encode_dc_group` primitive consumes WHOLE-IMAGE
#      token vectors (`dc_tokens: &[Token]`,
#      `ac_section_tokens_per_pass: &[Vec<Vec<Token>>]`). Token
#      collection currently happens whole-image in `encode_two_pass`,
#      then `encode_dc_group` just rearranges section emission. Real
#      per-DC-group memory savings require collecting tokens per-region
#      AND clustering at the end (the libjxl `global_group_codes[]`
#      shape change in commit `acc28c0`).
#
#   3. The default `encode_inner` already drops its biggest allocations
#      as early as the current architecture allows:
#        - masking:           line 1896 (after AC strategy)
#        - quant_field_float: line 2017 (after loop refinement)
#        - xyb_x/y/b:         line 2132 (after EPF sharpness)
#        - mask1x1:           line 2136 (after EPF sharpness)
#      The peak is structural: xyb + quant_field_float + mask1x1 + cfl
#      + ac_strategy must coexist between line 1302 (XYB convert) and
#      line 2132 (xyb drop) because each pipeline step reads from the
#      live xyb planes (chromacity, quant_field, mask1x1, gaborish, cfl
#      pass 1, ac_strategy, cfl pass 2, optional butt/ssim2/zensim
#      loops, transform_and_quantize, EPF sharpness).
#
# DEFAULT PATH PEAK RSS (this bench, fbm-ish content, default 2 GiB cap)
# =====================================================================
#   3072² (= 9.4 MP):  ~861-862 MiB — all 5 Buffering variants identical
#   4096² (= 16.8 MP): ~1527 MiB    — all 5 Buffering variants identical
#
#   bytes identical across variants (6973041 @ 3K, 12382528 @ 4K) →
#   confirms the Buffering knob is currently a no-op on the default
#   path. This is the backwards-compat guarantee — and the structural
#   gap that chunk 8 must close.
#
# RATE-CONTROL PATH PEAK RSS (this bench, 4K)
# ============================================
#   FullBuffered:   4441 MiB  bytes=7336845  (whole-image precompute)
#   Threshold2048:  4440 MiB  bytes=7336845  (also whole-image)
#   BufferedOutput: 4759 MiB  bytes=7340945  (per-region; +7% RSS)
#   FullStreaming:  4582 MiB  bytes=7340945  (per-region; +3% RSS)
#   Auto:           4712 MiB  bytes=7340945  (Auto > 2048² → per-region)
#
#   Bytes split into two classes (Δ +0.056% per-region vs whole-image)
#   confirms the chunk-6 dispatch matrix is correctly routing on the
#   `Buffering` value. The per-region class costs MORE peak RSS today
#   because of the xyb_pre_gaborish snapshot — same pattern as 3K.
#
# CHUNK 8 PLAN (the actual peak-RSS reduction)
# =============================================
#   To deliver the 2-3× peak-RSS reduction the prompt targets, chunk 8
#   must reshape `encode_inner` to NOT hold the whole image in memory at
#   any point:
#
#   1. Replace `encode_two_pass`'s whole-image token collection with a
#      per-DC-group token collector. Each DC group:
#        - Tokenizes its DC + AC + metadata into local `Vec<Token>`s.
#        - Pushes those into a per-region `EncodedDcGroup`.
#        - Drops its slice of `quant_dc / quant_ac / nzeros /
#          raw_nzeros / xyb_*` immediately after tokenization.
#      Mirrors libjxl's `OutputGroups` shape post-`acc28c0`.
#
#   2. Run histogram clustering ACROSS the accumulated per-DC-group
#      tokens (libjxl-parity: clustering still happens whole-image at
#      `buffering ∈ {0, 1, 2}`, only `buffering = 3` ships local trees
#      — and even then only for `responsive=1` modular, per `b3510d1` /
#      `1389871`).
#
#   3. Emit DC global + per-DC-group sections + AC global. For
#      `BufferedOutput`: natural-order TOC + `permuted_toc=0`
#      (libjxl `6553831` fix). For `FullStreaming`: permuted TOC with
#      seek-back via `WritableSeek` (chunk 6 wired the trait but the
#      actual streaming-output emit path is chunk 8).
#
#   4. Drop the global xyb slice for each DC group as soon as its
#      `encode_dc_group` returns. At 4K this brings the live working
#      set from ~190 MiB (whole xyb) down to ~5 MiB (one 256×256 ×
#      24 B/pixel DC-group footprint).
#
#   The structural shape exists today (`encode_dc_group` primitive,
#   `compute_with_budget_and_buffering` dispatch, `WritableSeek`
#   trait, `permuted_toc=0` test). The remaining work is per-DC-group
#   token collection + early per-region buffer drop in `encode_inner`.
#   Estimated 4-7 agent-days per the porting plan
#   (libjxl_streaming_refactor_porting_plan_2026-05-18.md → chunk 5).
#
# Why chunk 7 didn't attempt the half-refactor (honest-stop rationale)
# =====================================================================
# The prompt allowed "ship the partial refactor that at least removes
# the precompute peak even if downstream still re-materializes." The
# partial refactor (route precompute through compute_with_budget_and_-
# buffering) ADDS memory cost on the default path because of (1)
# above, not removes it. Shipping that as "chunk 7 progress" would be
# false-completion: the user-visible metric (peak RSS) would regress,
# and the BufferedOutput knob would still be a no-op on the byte-level
# (encode_inner re-does everything inline regardless of what the
# precomputed struct contains).
#
# The honest, useful chunk-7 deliverable is the 4K bench above plus
# this documented chunk-8 plan. The chunk-6 commit explicitly named
# chunk 7 as "Refactor encode_inner to call the same per-DC-group
# helpers"; this bench is the empirical confirmation that the
# refactor as-named cannot land without ALSO solving the per-DC-group
# token collection problem (which is chunk 8 scope).
